BT /F1 16 Tf 54 742 Td (The Lantern at North Pier) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 724 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 54 710 Td (The Lantern) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 696 Td (Mara found the brass lantern beneath a loose board in the old ferry house.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 682 Td (It was small enough to hold in one hand, but its glass was clear and bright.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 668 Td (A note tied to the handle said, Take this to the north pier before the fog) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 654 Td (comes in. No name followed, and no one in the village admitted leaving it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 640 Td (Mara lit the wick and watched a calm gold circle spread across the dusty floor.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 626 Td (Outside, gulls turned above the harbor, and the tide was already beginning to rise.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 612 Td (She remembered her grandmother saying that every harbor light was a promise:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 598 Td (someone was watching, and someone would find the shore. Mara tucked the note) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 584 Td (into her coat and closed the ferry house door behind her.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 570 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 54 556 Td (The Crossing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 542 Td (She carried the lantern along the seawall as evening settled over the roofs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 528 Td (At the north pier, a little wooden boat bumped softly against its rope.         An) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 514 Td (old man stood beside it, holding a map that the damp air had curled at         the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 500 Td (edges. He looked relieved when he saw the light. My sister is waiting         across) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 486 Td (the inlet, he explained. The fog hides the channel markers, and I         cannot) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 472 Td (leave without a guide. Mara set the lantern in the bow, where its         reflection) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 458 Td (made a narrow road across the dark water. The man offered her         the map, but) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 444 Td (she knew these waters from summers spent rowing with her father.         She pointed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 430 Td (toward the quiet gap between two black rocks and told him to keep         the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 416 Td (lantern in sight. Then she pushed the boat gently away from the pier.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 402 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 54 388 Td (A Safe Return) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 374 Td (The boat moved slowly, following the lantern's trembling path. From the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 360 Td (shore, Mara could just make out a second light answering from the far bank.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 346 Td (The old man raised one hand, and the boat turned toward it. When it reached) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 332 Td (the landing, a woman stepped forward and laughed with joy. They had been) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 318 Td (apart for many years, but they recognized each other at once. Mara waited) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 304 Td (until both were safely ashore, then carried the empty lantern home. At dawn) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 290 Td (she found a fresh note beneath her door: The light is yours whenever someone) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 276 Td (needs help finding the way. This time, it bore no signature either.         Mara) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 262 Td (cleaned the lantern and placed it by the window, ready for another night.) Tj ET
